Subject: [PATCH] net: airoha: admit short OMCI to its authenticated parser

Keep the Ethernet minimum and reject CRC, oversize and aggregation errors.
The PON consumer validates the OMCI wire length, session, GEM and MIC.

--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_pon.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_pon.c
@@ -86,7 +86,11 @@
 static int airoha_pon_rx_meta(const u32 words[4], struct airoha_pon_rx_meta *meta)
 {
 	/* Never feed an aggregated or malformed frame to a raw PON consumer. */
-	if ((words[0] & GENMASK(13, 11)) ||
+	/* The Ethernet minimum also marks valid short OMCI as runt. Only
+	 * OMCI may pass that bit; its consumer verifies length/session/MIC.
+	 */
+	if ((words[0] & (BIT(13) | BIT(11))) ||
+	    ((words[0] & BIT(12)) && !(words[0] & BIT(8))) ||
 	    FIELD_GET(QDMA_ETH_RXMSG_AGG_COUNT_MASK, words[2]) > 1)
 		return -EBADMSG;
 	memcpy(meta->words, words, sizeof(meta->words));
